# Pulled Kaggle session output.
# `kaggle_session --pull` downloads everything a notebook left in /kaggle/working, which
# includes the staged LoRA checkpoints and four copies of tokenizer.json — 420 MB and
# ~1.25M lines for session 02i alone. It is a local cache of something the Kaggle session
# already holds, so committing it costs a lot and preserves nothing.
#
# The findings from these runs ARE version-controlled: the reports, per-language CSVs and
# diagnosis JSON are copied into research/evaluation/results/, and the modules that
# produced them into research/code/. Curate into research/, never commit the raw pull.
files_v3/kaggle_runs/results_*/
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
optimizer.pt
scheduler.pt

# Corpora. Regenerable from Samanantar by dataset_generator.py + relabel_dataset.py, and
# large enough (train.phonemes.jsonl is 31 MB) that git is the wrong place for them.
data/
augmented_dataset/
*.jsonl
!research/**/*.jsonl
